# The same construct as test_nilpy_a_module_qualified_def_is_a_value.npy, with
# the value read performed INSIDE AN IMPORTED MODULE instead of in the program.
# It is a different question and needs its own file, for two reasons:
#
# THE SCAN'S WINDOW. PyDefUsedAsValue runs from token 0 to MainProgramTokCount,
# and MainProgramTokCount is RE-POINTED to whichever module is being parsed. A
# read in a module lexed EARLIER is in range; a read in one lexed later is not.
# This program therefore imports ONLY the reader, so the reader's tokens exist
# before the module holding the defs is parsed. The other import order is a
# known hole and has its own ticket
# (bug-n-a-qualified-def-value-read-is-invisible-when-the-def-s-module-is-parsed-first)
# -- deliberately not exercised here, because a fixture that passes in one order
# and fails in the other must not be written in the order that passes.
#
# CONTAMINATION. If the program ALSO read these defs, the program's own read
# would normalise them and the module's rows would pass for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the module. Every def this file reaches is read only from
# inside retkreader.
import retkreader

print(repr(retkreader.read_in_a_module()))
print(repr(retkreader.two().fittings()))
print(repr(retkreader.three().fittings()))
